1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,580
Good morning everyone. My name's Janet Parker and I'm the human resources manager.

2
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:13,672
We're very happy to welcome you to your new apprenticeship.

3
00:00:13,672 --> 00:00:20,220
I hope that the next six months will be a positive and enjoyable experience for you.

4
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:25,780
I'd like to start with some general advice about being an apprentice.

5
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:32,230
Most of you have very little or no experience of working for a big organisation

6
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:36,530
and the first week or so may be quite challenging.

7
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:40,060
There will be a lot of new information to take in

8
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:45,000
but don't worry too much about trying to remember everything.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,774
The important thing is to check with someone if you're not sure what to do -

10
00:00:51,774 --> 00:00:54,580
you'll find your supervisor is very approachable

11
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:59,000
and won't mind explaining things or helping you out.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You're here to learn so make the most of that opportunity.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,632
You'll be spending time in different departments during your first week

14
00:01:08,632 --> 00:01:14,947
so make an effort to talk to as many people as possible about their work -

15
00:01:14,947 --> 00:01:20,000
you'll make some new friends and find out lots of useful information.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,560
As well as having a supervisor, you'll each be assigned a mentor.

17
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,781
This person will be someone

18
00:01:27,781 --> 00:01:30,300
who's recently completed an apprenticeship

19
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,000
and you'll meet with them on a weekly basis.

20
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,410
Their role is to provide help and support throughout your apprenticeship.

21
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:44,991
Of course, this doesn't mean they actually do any of your work for you -

22
00:01:44,991 --> 00:01:49,775
instead they'll be asking you about what goals you've achieved so far,

23
00:01:49,775 --> 00:01:54,160
as well as helping you to identify any areas for improvement.

24
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:59,500
You can also discuss your more long-term ambitions with them as well.

25
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:06,579
Now I just want to run through a few company policies for our apprenticeship scheme

26
00:02:06,579 --> 00:02:09,410
with you. Most importantly, the internet.

27
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:15,000
As part of your job you'll be doing some research online so obviously

28
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,932
you'll have unlimited access for that

29
00:02:17,932 --> 00:02:24,660
but please don't use it for personal use - you'll have your own phones for that.

30
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:29,270
Some of you have already asked me about flexible working.

31
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:35,180
After your probationary three-month period - some of you will be eligible for this -

32
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:38,560
but it will depend on which department you're in

33
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:42,000
and what your personal circumstances are.

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,570
So please don't assume you'll automatically be permitted to do this.

35
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:52,670
I want to make sure there's no confusion about our holiday policy.

36
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:55,900
Apart from any statutory public holidays

37
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:03,390
we ask that you don't book any holidays until after your six-month apprenticeship has finished.

38
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:07,307
Time off should only be taken if you are unwell.

39
00:03:07,307 --> 00:03:12,400
Please speak to your supervisor if this is going to be a problem.

40
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,960
You'll be expected to work a 40-hour week

41
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:21,760
but there may be opportunities to do overtime during busy periods.

42
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:24,660
Although you're not required to do this,

43
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:31,290
it can be a valuable experience - so we advise you to take it up if possible.

44
00:03:31,290 --> 00:03:35,876
Obviously, we understand that people do have commitments outside work,

45
00:03:35,876 --> 00:03:40,920
so don't worry if there are times when you are unavailable.

46
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:45,537
As you know, we don't have a formal dress code here -

47
00:03:45,537 --> 00:03:49,734
you may wear casual clothes as long as they're practical -

48
00:03:49,734 --> 00:03:56,870
and the only restriction for shoes we have is on high heels for health and safety reasons.

49
00:03:56,870 --> 00:04:00,870
Comfortable shoes like trainers are preferable.

50
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:04,520
There's a heavily subsidised canteen on site

51
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:08,890
where you can get hot meals or salads cheaply.

52
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:11,740
Snacks and drinks are also provided

53
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:17,310
so we've decided to introduce a no packed lunch policy.

54
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:21,569
This is partly to encourage healthy eating at work

55
00:04:21,569 --> 00:04:27,720
and partly to stop people from eating at their workstation, which is unhygienic.

56
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,000
OK moving on to...
